amdxdna: keep WRITE32-only RTP on the PARTIAL_ELF layer chain

Empty host patch tables are valid: a TXN of npu.write32 has no DDR relocations.
Requiring a non-empty table forced those programs onto START_NPU, which splits
them out of the PARTIAL_ELF layer group. Windows Path-B then submits the
context-length WRITE32 as a separate native command, so the first attention
child of the next chain can observe the previous token's RTP.

Treat an empty patch table as PARTIAL_ELF-eligible so FLM's gen_set_context
run accumulates as child 0 of the same runlist as the layers that read it.
